
# FilmLog — Full-Stack (v2)

An extended, production-ready version of FilmLog featuring secure JWT authentication, a .NET Core backend that proxies the OMDb movie API, full relational database persistence, and a statistics dashboard. Built for INF 354 Assignment 3 at the University of Pretoria.

## What It Does

- **Secure authentication** — Register and login with JWT Bearer Token; passwords hashed with BCrypt
- **Movie search** — Frontend calls the backend, which proxies requests to OMDb API (API key protected server-side)
- **Watchlist & Watched List** — All user data stored in a relational database (not local storage)
- **Statistics Dashboard** — Pie chart of top genres, a custom bar chart, and a summary table based on the user's watched movies
- **Unit Tests** — Backend tests covering successful (HTTP 200) and unsuccessful (HTTP 404) requests

## Tech Stack

**Backend:**
- ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 8)
- Entity Framework Core (Code-First, SQL Server)
- JWT Bearer Token authentication
- BCrypt.Net password hashing
- OMDb API integration (`https://www.omdbapi.com`)
- xUnit + Moq

**Frontend:**
- Ionic / Angular
- Angular `HttpClient` with JWT interceptor
- Chart.js / ng2-charts (statistics dashboard)
- TypeScript, SCSS

## Architecture

```
Backend (ASP.NET Core)
├── /api/auth/register      POST — register new user
├── /api/auth/login         POST — login, returns JWT token
├── /api/movies/search      GET  — proxy to OMDb API
├── /api/watchlist          GET, POST, DELETE — user's watchlist (protected)
└── /api/watched            GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, POST/reset — watched list (protected)

Frontend (Ionic/Angular)
├── Login / Register        JWT stored in Local Storage
├── Search                  Calls backend /api/movies/search
├── Watchlist               HTTP calls to protected backend endpoints
├── Watched                 HTTP calls; times-watched counter; reset button
└── Statistics Dashboard    Pie chart (top genres), bar chart, summary table
```

## Database Schema

| Table | Key Fields |
|-------|------------|
| Users | Id, Email, PasswordHash, CreatedAt |
| WatchlistItems | Id, UserId (FK), Title, Year, Poster, Actors, Genre |
| WatchedItems | Id, UserId (FK), Title, Year, Poster, Actors, Genre, TimesWatched |

## How to Run

### Backend

**Prerequisites:** Visual Studio 2022, .NET 8 SDK, SQL Server

1. Open the backend solution in Visual Studio 2022
2. Add your OMDb API key to `appsettings.json`:
   ```json
   "OmdbApiKey": "your_api_key_here"
   ```
3. Run migrations:
   ```
   Add-Migration InitialCreate
   Update-Database
   ```
4. Press **F5** to start the API

### Frontend

```bash
cd filmlog-frontend
npm install
ionic serve
```

